---
title: Skills
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /skills/
wide: true
changeFreq: weekly
description: Nine Claude Code skills for product engineering work, from planning and code review to dependency patching, deploys, and growth. Free and open source.
---

{%- set repoUrl = skillsRepo.url -%}
{%- set linkClass = "text-accent dark:text-orange-400 underline decoration-accent/30 dark:decoration-orange-400/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent dark:hover:decoration-orange-400 transition-all" -%}
{%- set eyebrowClass = "text-[0.8125rem] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400" -%}

<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6">

  <section class="mb-16">
    <p class="{{ eyebrowClass }}">Claude Code skills</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-none">Skills</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg sm:text-xl leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
      {{ skills.items.length }} skills I use to do product engineering with an agent: plan the work,
      review it, keep it patched, ship it, and then get people to find it. Each one is a single
      markdown file, and each ships as a slash command.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <a href="#install" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-md bg-ink px-4 py-2 text-[0.9375rem] font-medium text-paper no-underline hover:bg-accent dark:bg-stone-100 dark:text-stone-900 dark:hover:bg-orange-400 transition-colors">Install</a>
      <a href="{{ repoUrl }}" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md border border-line px-4 py-2 text-[0.9375rem] text-ink no-underline hover:border-accent/40 hover:text-accent dark:border-stone-700 dark:text-stone-200 dark:hover:border-orange-400/40 dark:hover:text-orange-400 transition-colors" data-track="skills_github_click">
        <svg class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 .3a12 12 0 00-3.8 23.4c.6.1.8-.3.8-.6v-2.2c-3.3.7-4-1.6-4-1.6-.6-1.4-1.4-1.8-1.4-1.8-1-.7.1-.7.1-.7 1.2.1 1.8 1.2 1.8 1.2 1 1.8 2.8 1.3 3.5 1 0-.8.4-1.3.7-1.6-2.7-.3-5.5-1.3-5.5-5.9 0-1.3.5-2.4 1.2-3.2-.1-.3-.5-1.5.1-3.2 0 0 1-.3 3.3 1.2a11.5 11.5 0 016 0c2.3-1.5 3.3-1.2 3.3-1.2.6 1.7.2 2.9.1 3.2.8.8 1.2 1.9 1.2 3.2 0 4.6-2.8 5.6-5.5 5.9.4.4.8 1.1.8 2.2v3.3c0 .3.2.7.8.6A12 12 0 0012 .3"/></svg>
        <span>{{ skillsRepo.repo }}</span>
        {% if skillsRepo.stars %}
          <span class="flex items-center gap-1 border-l border-line pl-2 text-stone-600 dark:border-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
            <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2.5l2.9 6.1 6.6.8-4.9 4.6 1.3 6.6L12 17.3l-5.9 3.3 1.3-6.6-4.9-4.6 6.6-.8z"/></svg>
            {{ skillsRepo.stars }}<span class="sr-only"> stars</span>
          </span>
        {% else %}
          <span class="border-l border-line pl-2 text-stone-600 dark:border-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">Star it</span>
        {% endif %}
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="install" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-10">
    <h2 class="{{ eyebrowClass }} border-b border-line dark:border-stone-800 pb-3 mb-6">Install</h2>

    {%- set installs = [
      {
        "title": "Claude Code plugin",
        "note": "All nine skills in one plugin. Run these inside Claude Code, then /reload-plugins.",
        "commands": ["/plugin marketplace add joshghent/skills", "/plugin install joshghent-skills@joshghent-skills"]
      },
      {
        "title": "Skills CLI",
        "note": "Pick one skill and install it into Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, or any agent the skills CLI supports.",
        "commands": ["npx skills add joshghent/skills --skill groundwork"]
      }
    ] -%}

    <div class="grid gap-5">
      {% for install in installs %}
        <div class="min-w-0 rounded-lg border border-line dark:border-stone-800 p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold tracking-tight text-ink dark:text-stone-100">{{ install.title }}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">{{ install.note }}</p>
          <div class="mt-4 space-y-2">
            {% for command in install.commands %}
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-[#282420] pl-3 pr-1.5 py-1.5 dark:bg-stone-950">
                <code class="min-w-0 flex-1 overflow-x-auto whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-[#e8e4de]">{{ command }}</code>
                <button type="button" class="shrink-0 rounded px-2 py-1 font-sans text-xs text-stone-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white transition-colors" data-copy-url="{{ command }}" data-track="skills_install_copy" aria-label="Copy command: {{ command }}">
                  <span data-copy-label>Copy</span>
                </button>
              </div>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
      Keep them current with <code class="rounded bg-surface px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.875em] dark:bg-stone-800">/plugin marketplace update joshghent-skills</code>.
      Or skip the tooling: copy any skill folder into <code class="rounded bg-surface px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.875em] dark:bg-stone-800">~/.claude/skills/</code>.
      Everything is on <a href="{{ repoUrl }}" class="{{ linkClass }}">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="{{ eyebrowClass }} border-b border-line dark:border-stone-800 pb-3 mb-6">What is a skill?</h2>
    <p class="max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
      A skill is a markdown file of instructions that an agent loads when a request matches it. It
      is the difference between asking for a code review and handing over the checklist you would
      use yourself.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold tracking-tight text-ink dark:text-stone-100">The problem</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
          Ask an agent to "update the dependencies" and you get a different process each time.
          It forgets the build, skips the tests, or bumps a major version in the same PR as a
          security fix. You end up re-explaining how you want it done, every time.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold tracking-tight text-ink dark:text-stone-100">The fix</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
          Write the process down once. A skill sets out the steps, what to check, what never to
          do, and what the output should look like. The agent follows it the same way on every
          repo, and you can trigger it with one slash command.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold tracking-tight text-ink dark:text-stone-100">Why it compounds</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
          When a run goes wrong, you fix the skill rather than the prompt. That lesson then
          applies to every future run, on every project. Over a few months the skill holds
          more of your judgement than you could type out on any single day.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="all-skills" class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="{{ eyebrowClass }} border-b border-line dark:border-stone-800 pb-3 mb-8">The skills</h2>

    <div class="space-y-12">
      {% for group in skills.groups %}
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400" aria-hidden="true">{{ loop.index | padStart(2, "0") }}</span>
            <h3 id="{{ group.id }}" class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink dark:text-stone-100">{{ group.title }}</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">{{ group.summary }}</p>

          <ul class="mt-5 grid list-none gap-4 p-0 sm:grid-cols-2">
            {% for skill in skills.items | filterBy("group", group.id) %}
              <li id="{{ skill.name }}" class="flex min-w-0 flex-col rounded-lg border border-line dark:border-stone-800 p-5 scroll-mt-10">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-3.5">
                  <span class="flex h-10 w-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-accent/10 text-accent dark:bg-orange-400/10 dark:text-orange-400">
                    {% set skillName = skill.name %}{% include "components/skill-icon.njk" %}
                  </span>
                  <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2">
                      <h4 class="font-bold tracking-tight text-ink dark:text-stone-100">{{ skill.name }}</h4>
                      {% if skill.added | daysSince < 45 %}<span class="rounded bg-accent/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-sans text-xs font-medium text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-400/10 dark:text-orange-200">New</span>{% endif %}
                    </div>
                    <p class="font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">/{{ skill.name }}</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-3 flex-1 text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">{{ skill.summary }}</p>
                <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-[0.9375rem]">
                  <a href="{{ skills.source }}/{{ skill.name }}/SKILL.md" class="{{ linkClass }}" data-track="skills_source_click">Read the skill<span class="sr-only">: {{ skill.name }}</span></a>
                  {% if skill.link %}<a href="{{ skill.link.href }}" class="{{ linkClass }}">{{ skill.link.label }}<span class="sr-only"> about {{ skill.name }}</span></a>{% endif %}
                </div>
              </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="changelog" class="scroll-mt-10">
    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between border-b border-line dark:border-stone-800 pb-3 mb-8">
      <h2 class="{{ eyebrowClass }}">What&rsquo;s changed</h2>
      <a href="{{ repoUrl }}/commits/main" class="text-sm no-underline text-stone-500 hover:text-accent dark:text-stone-400 dark:hover:text-orange-400 transition-colors">Full history &rarr;</a>
    </div>

    <ol class="list-none p-0 m-0">
      {% for release in skills.changelog %}
        <li class="relative grid gap-2 pb-8 sm:grid-cols-[9rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
          <div class="sm:text-right">
            <time datetime="{{ release.date }}" class="text-[0.9375rem] text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">{{ release.date | fromISO }}</time>
            {% if release.version %}<p class="font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">v{{ release.version }}</p>{% endif %}
          </div>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-3 border-l border-line pl-5 m-0 dark:border-stone-800">
            {% for change in release.changes %}
              <li class="text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
                {% if change.skills.length %}
                  {% for name in change.skills %}<a href="#{{ name }}" class="mr-1.5 rounded bg-surface px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-ink no-underline hover:text-accent dark:bg-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 dark:hover:text-orange-400">{{ name }}</a>{% endfor %}
                {% else %}
                  <span class="mr-1.5 rounded bg-surface px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.8125rem] text-stone-600 dark:bg-stone-800 dark:text-stone-300">plugin</span>
                {% endif %}
                {% if change.type == "new" %}<span class="mr-1 font-sans text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-accent dark:text-orange-400">New</span>{% endif %}
                {{ change.text }}
              </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>

</div>
